    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalism employs methodologies like Original Intent (what the Framers subjectively desired) or Original Public Meaning (what ordinary people at the time understood the text to mean); this method prioritizes fixed historical anchors despite textual ambiguities. Living constitutionalists utilize methodologies like evolving societal norms or purposivism, viewing the text as a principle whose application must adapt to current governmental and social contexts. While originalism aims for stability by constraining judicial discretion within historical parameters, living constitutionalism offers greater adaptability, though its reliance on evolving norms can lead to less predictable rulings.",
      "source": "target",
